# Citation metadata for CCDB (https://citation-file-format.github.io). GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository".
# The version follows ccdb.version.version; python/tests/unit_test_metadata_files.py checks that they agree.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CCDB in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "CCDB: Calibration Constants Database"
abstract: >-
  CCDB stores and manages the calibration constants of nuclear and high energy physics experiments.
  Constants are looked up by run number in a tree of tables, with variations for alternative sets,
  the complete history of every change, and named snapshot tags. CCDB provides C++ and Python
  APIs, a command line tool and a web interface over MySQL, MariaDB and SQLite databases.
authors:
  - family-names: Romanov
    given-names: Dmitry
    email: romanov@jlab.org
    affiliation: Thomas Jefferson National Accelerator Facility
version: 2.5.0
license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/JeffersonLab/ccdb"
url: "https://jeffersonlab.github.io/ccdb"
keywords:
  - calibration
  - conditions database
  - nuclear physics
  - high energy physics
  - Jefferson Lab
